## Mapping Names to Scores

A **Map** associates keys with values. Think of it as a dictionary: you look up a name (key) to find their score (value).

### Building the Scoreboard

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let leaderboard: Map[Str, Int] = Map[Str, Int].new();
  leaderboard.insert("Alice", 850);
  leaderboard.insert("Bob", 920);
  leaderboard.insert("Carol", 780);
  leaderboard.insert("Dave", 950);

  io.println("Bob's score: " + string.int_to_str(
    match leaderboard.get(&"Bob") {
      Some(s) => s,
      None => 0,
    }
  ));
  return 0;
}
```

`.insert(key, value)` adds an entry. `.get(&key)` returns `Some(value)` or `None` if the key is missing.

### Finding Top 3 with a While Loop

Maps are unordered, so we need a Vec of names to iterate through. Then we find the highest unscored player, record them, and repeat:

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let scores: Map[Str, Int] = Map[Str, Int].new();
  let names: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();

  names.push("Alice"); scores.insert("Alice", 850);
  names.push("Bob");   scores.insert("Bob", 920);
  names.push("Carol"); scores.insert("Carol", 780);
  names.push("Dave");  scores.insert("Dave", 950);

  let used: Map[Str, Bool] = Map[Str, Bool].new();
  let rank = 0;
  while rank < 3 {
    let best_name = "";
    let best_score = -1;
    let j = 0;
    while j < names.len() {
      let name = match names.get(j) { Some(n) => n, None => "" };
      let score = match scores.get(&name) { Some(s) => s, None => -1 };
      let already = used.contains(&name);
      if score > best_score & !already {
        best_score = score;
        best_name = name;
      }
      j = j + 1;
    }
    used.insert(best_name, true);
    io.println(string.int_to_str(rank + 1) + ". " + best_name + " - " + string.int_to_str(best_score));
    rank = rank + 1;
  }
  return 0;
}
```

Each pass finds the highest remaining score, marks the winner as used, and moves to the next rank.

